=== SURVEY ===
Web source AiLimitBanner.tsx is a FULLY-CONTROLLED, presentational `AlertBanner`. The parent owns
the data (the `limit: AiLimitInfo | null` from `useAiStream`) and the handlers (onRetry,
onUseBaseline, onDismiss); the banner renders nothing when info==null. When info!=null it shows:
  • variant by bannerLevel: '' → info, 'warn' → warning, 'critical' → danger (web `variant`).
  • a reason-keyed title + description via the `titleForReason` / `descriptionForReason` switch
    tables (12 reasons incl. the grouped input_tokens|output_tokens and
    missing_feature_id|unknown_feature_id, plus the generic default).
  • a live "Try again in Ns" line while secondsLeft>0 — the ONLY internal state, driven by a 1s
    setInterval whose effect deps are [info] (reset on a new limit).
  • "Use baseline" (when onUseBaseline && baselineAvailable) and "Retry" (when onRetry && retryReady)
    buttons, plus an optional dismiss (onClose).
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation (the info + handlers are props, not a fetch).
Shared components: @/components/feedback (AlertBanner) → TSAlertBanner; @/components/ui/Button → TSButton.
Charts/maps: none.
i18n keys extracted from source: ai.limit.useBaseline, ai.limit.retry, ai.limit.retryIn, and the
  title.*/desc.* taxonomy (costCap, costCapUnavailable, settingsUnavailable, burst, perMinute,
  perDay, tokens, providerUnavailable, featureMisconfigured, generic) — all reproduced verbatim.
Existing native: a public `AiLimitInfo` (exact web shape) already exists module-wide
  (shared-surfaces/AIAutoTripNameSuggestion.Adapter.swift, surface 0007). REUSED it — redeclaring
  would be a duplicate-symbol collision (the very defect class blocking the sibling slots below).
  No AiLimitBanner*/AiLimitSeverity/AiLimitReasonCopy/AiLimitConnection/AiLimitTicker symbol existed
  (collision-checked, all 0).

=== REASONING ===
- The web banner is parent-controlled + synchronous; the prompt requires a production-polished native
  surface reproducing its DATA, composition, states, and i18n, with every state visible (no blank box).
  Chosen architecture mirrors the canonical P4 leaf (AnnouncerRegion / AICostForecastNarration):
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): AiLimitSeverity (bannerLevel→variant + SF Symbol), AiLimitCopy +
    AiLimitReasonCopy (the reason taxonomy as a static table with alias normalization = the web grouped
    cases + default), AiLimitCountdown (initial/tick/isRetryReady/retryInText — the web secondsLeft
    arithmetic + interpolation), AiLimitBannerAccessibility (combined VoiceOver label, terminal-
    punctuation aware).
  • Model: AiLimitBannerTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; AiLimitConnection axis;
    AiLimitBannerCapabilities (which handlers exist = web optional props); AiLimitBannerInput snapshot
    (controlled AiLimitInfo + parent lifecycle); AiLimitBannerResolved + Projection (loading/empty/
    error/data + affordance gating); @Observable AiLimitBannerModel (binds source, drives the countdown
    through the AiLimitTicker, resets only when the info VALUE changes — a connection-only update does
    NOT restart a running timer — one-shot stale auto-refresh, handler-gated retry/baseline/dismiss);
    AiLimitBannerStrings i18n facade (table "AiLimitBanner").
  • Seams: AiLimitBannerSource protocol; StaticAiLimitBannerSource (production — the controlled `info`
    prop, re-emitted on start/refresh/update); InMemoryAiLimitBannerSource (previews/tests);
    AiLimitTicker (TimerAiLimitTicker production 1Hz; ManualAiLimitTicker test double).
  • View/Views/States + Previews + strings + Tests/ModelTests.
- States rendered (no hidden surface): loading (skeleton banner), empty (no active limit — friendly
  TSEmptyState, the native parity of the web `return null`, never blank), error (retry — web QueryError
  peer), data (the active limit banner: TSAlertBanner severity chrome + reason title/description + the
  live countdown line + Use-baseline/Retry/dismiss affordances), and the orthogonal connection axis
  stale/offline (freshness chip + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition).
- Accessibility: every interactive control is a standalone TSButton with its own VoiceOver label
  (rendered beneath the combined TSAlertBanner chrome so each affordance stays individually focusable);
  Dynamic Type via tokens; the freshness chip is a labeled button.

